  "body": "Brand New Coastal Luxury\r\nSet on Murrays Bay's coveted Beach Road, this brand-new architectural home offers a rare combination of contemporary design, premium finishes and an unbeatable coastal address on Auckland's North Shore.\r\n\r\nThe Home:\r\nSpanning approximately 274.67m² across a freehold site of approximately 510m², this beautifully appointed four-bedroom, four-bathroom residence has been finished to an exacting standard throughout. Expect light-filled open-plan living, premium fixtures and fittings, and a design that flows effortlessly between indoor and outdoor spaces — perfect for entertaining or simply enjoying the North Shore lifestyle. With four generous bedrooms and four well-appointed bathrooms, there's space and privacy for family, guests, or a home office. Being brand new, every detail — from the kitchen through to the landscaping — is untouched and ready for its first owner to move straight in and enjoy.\r\n\r\nThe Location:\r\nBeach Road is one of Murrays Bay's most sought-after streets, running along the elevated coastline with a genuine sense of place and community. This is a suburb defined by its relationship with the sea — homes near Beach Road and the cliff-edge streets overlooking the Hauraki Gulf carry a distinctly coastal character, and this\r\naddress puts you right in the heart of it.\r\n\r\nYou're just moments from Murrays Bay Beach and Wharf, a favourite for swimming, paddleboarding, sailing and simply watching the ferries glide past Rangitoto. Residents here enjoy easy access to lifestyle activities such as sailing, walking, swimming, tennis and bowls, all within a genuine, tight-knit community feel that's hard to find so close to the city.\r\n\r\nSchools:\r\nFamilies are exceptionally well served in this pocket of the North Shore. The suburb's identity is strongly tied to Rangitoto College zoning, one of the country's largest and most respected state colleges, while Murrays Bay Intermediate and the local Murrays Bay Primary School — set in a beautiful location overlooking the Hauraki Gulf and Rangitoto Island — round out an excellent zoning package right on your doorstep. For those considering private schooling, Kristin, Westminster Christian School and Pinehurst are all within the wider area.\r\n\r\nGetting Around:\r\nBeach Road connects easily to Murrays Bay's local roads and on to the wider North Shore network, with the Northern Busway corridor and nearby Albany Station providing fast public transport access into Auckland's CBD. Regular bus services also run directly to Takapuna and the Auckland city centre, making the daily commute straightforward whether you drive or take public transport — with the CBD comfortably reachable in around 25–30 minutes outside peak times.\r\n\r\nThe Community:\r\nMurrays Bay retains a lovely village charm — it's primarily a residential area but does have its own community centre, restaurant and café, while neighbouring Browns Bay and Mairangi Bay offer a fuller range of shops, cafés and beachfront dining just a short drive away. With native bush, coastal walkways and a genuine community\r\nspirit, this is East Coast Bays living at its best.\r\n\r\nBrand new. Beachside. Beautifully finished. An outstanding opportunity to secure a turn-key family home in one of the North Shore's most desirable coastal streets.\r\n\r\nContact us today to arrange a private viewing.",
